{
  "$comment": [
    "Named, opt-in binding profiles. A profile adds parameter->category bindings",
    "ON TOP OF the corporate baseline in CATEGORY_BINDINGS.csv, for projects that",
    "switch it on. A project that does not enable a profile is unaffected.",
    "",
    "Enable per project by listing ids in <project>/_BIM_COORD/binding_profiles.json:",
    "    { \"enabled\": [\"lps-natural-components\"] }",
    "",
    "WHY THIS EXISTS. LoadSharedParamsCommand binds each parameter to ITS OWN",
    "category set precisely so discipline data does not leak across categories.",
    "Some parameters legitimately need a WIDE category set, but only in the",
    "minority of projects that use the feature - binding them corporately would",
    "put them on every element of those categories in every project."
  ],
  "profiles": [
    {
      "id": "lps-natural-components",
      "name": "LPS natural components (BS EN 62305-3 reuse)",
      "description": "Binds the lightning-protection parameters to the structural and architectural categories that a BS EN 62305-3 system may REUSE as natural components - foundation rebar as a Type B earth electrode, a metal roof or metallic facade as a natural air termination. Required by the three Multi-Category LPS reuse tag families; without it those tags place and render blank.",
      "requiredBy": [
        "STING - LPS Foundation Earth (Structural Reuse) Tag",
        "STING - LPS Natural Air Termination (Architectural Reuse) Tag",
        "STING - LPS Generic Component Tag"
      ],
      "bindings": [
        {
          "param": "ELC_LPS_EARTH_TAG_TXT",
          "categories": [
            "Structural Foundations",
            "Structural Rebar",
            "Structural Area Reinforcement",
            "Structural Path Reinforcement",
            "Structural Fabric Reinforcement"
          ]
        },
        {
